# Read by the `ignore` crate (and by ripgrep/fd), NOT by git — which is exactly the point.
#
# Conformance fixture corpora are deliberately-flawed test data: checked into
# git and exercised by the conformance harness's own `cargo test` run, but excluded from
# kndo's self-check of its own repo (ROADMAP M1 exit: "kndo check on kndo's own JS-free repo
# returns cleanly"). Analyzing them would report every flaw they were written to contain.
#
# This lived in .gitignore until it silently skipped a newly added fixture — green locally,
# absent from CI, because .gitignore governs `git add` for untracked files. `.ignore` carries
# the same globs to every consumer that needs them and none of the version-control side
# effect, so the exclusion is stated once and means only what it says.
**/tests/fixtures/

# The v1 quarry: source the v2 rewrite mines for fixtures and oracle comparisons,
# no longer the code under self-analysis. kndo's dogfood judges v2 — the kndo being
# built — and these directories retire from the repo at the root swap.
/crates/
/xtask/
/action/
/examples/
/spikes/

# Frozen v2 experiment records (M-1 fingerprint spike): kept as evidence for the
# decision they measured, not product code.
/v2/spikes/

# Oracle output and corpus measurements: JSON captured from real runs, not code.
/v2/oracle/
/v2/corpus-findings/

# Third-party source vendored verbatim for one build-flag fix (its README records the
# one deviation): not the code under judgment, and its manifest is not ours to align.
/v2/vendor/
